Project: Kelasa Mitra, a voice-first job and skill matcher for blue-collar and gig workers in Bengaluru (IBM Bobathon: Build for Bengaluru, theme: More Opportunity, Greater Together).
Required IBM products: IBM Bob (builds everything) and IBM watsonx Orchestrate (the agent layer).
Stack: Python FastAPI, SQLite, React 18 + Vite + Tailwind 4 + Framer Motion, browser Web Speech API.
Core logic is deterministic: rule-based extraction, scoring, and template reasons in en/kn/hi. Numbers never come from an LLM.
Groq is an optional runtime LLM behind the provider module, with the rule-based fallback always working. No Google, no watsonx.ai, no paid services, no credit card.
Synthetic data only, always labelled "sample data". No real personal data, no stored audio, no children's data, no government IDs. Never commit API keys; .env stays in .gitignore.
Design: mobile-first, warm teal/marigold/cream, 48px touch targets, prefers-reduced-motion respected.
Make small changes. Run pytest after each task and show raw output with exit code. Do not add features I did not ask for.